  "task": {
    "objective": "Bring shared wetland crop/fish goods to markets while coordinating flood pulses, filtering reeds, crop diversity, shelters and tools. Every household seeks at least one sale after the first seasonal interval.",
    "natural_termination": "At t>=96 all twenty households have at least one sale; otherwise H=768. Failed, spoiled and flood-lost harvests remain actual outcomes.",
    "interaction": "Opening a gate drains its own pool and sends water downstream. Flood pulses bring fish/nutrients but destroy ripe crops; reed cutting opens boat routes while weakening filtering. Opposite-bank rack holders create a real crossing and dry cargo; complementary net holders catch fish. Neighbor seed diversity and bird shelters change future crop growth. Local exchange moves tools, seeds and perishables.",
